WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
In Ethiopia, at Lalibela, whole
churches were carved from solid rock.

2
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.140
Their builders planned
them as a new Jerusalem.

3
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:14.100
Far to the north, in medieval Europe,
popes claimed authority over kings,

4
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.810
and monks copied books by hand.

5
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.780
So how did faith in a crucified
teacher come to shape popes,

6
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.500
monks and an African kingdom?

7
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.350
In this mission, you'll learn what
Christians believe about Jesus,

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.790
from the Trinity to the resurrection.

9
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.450
Then you'll trace
Christianity across Europe,

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.360
Africa and Asia.

11
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.380
Your mission: find out how
one faith came to shape popes,

12
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.750
monks and an African kingdom.
